---
description: Design, verify, playtest and operationalize a safe escape-room graph.
args:{ sourceRecord: EscapeRoomProject; sourceEvidence: EvidenceItem[];room:EscapeRoomState;change:string[];proof:PuzzleProof}
returns:EscapeOperationsPacket
---
Read `creativeBrief`, `venueId`, `propIds`, `designerId` and `targetDurationMinutes` from the top level of the EscapeRoomProject record. Carry its accessibility route and puzzle prerequisites into the graph; do not replace them with a default room skeleton. Carry every source fact and evidence ref into the analysis branch that depends on it; when any transformed proposal conflicts with this anchor, hold that branch for review instead of accepting the placeholder.

Bind constraints = `modelRoomConstraints(room.brief, room.props, change, sourceRecord, sourceEvidence)`. Fictional stakes do not suspend actual exit, accessibility or staff intervention. Bind computedProof = `verifyPuzzleGraph(room, sourceEvidence)` from the source-owned structural, frontier and egress checks. Bind suppliedCheck = `reconcileProof(computedProof, proof)`; retain the external proof as corroboration only. If the supplied proof differs, the room revision mismatches, structure has duplicate IDs or invalid references, goals are unreachable, any terminal state is soft-locked, a required prop is unavailable, a prerequisite cycle blocks a goal, or egress is unverified, bind blocked = `blockInvalidPuzzleRoom(room, computedProof, suppliedCheck)` and return that complete blocked packet before authoring clue flavor. Never substitute supplied proof fields for computed results.

Bind clueReview = `auditClueFairness(room, computedProof)`. Check that information is discoverable before each required action, that plausible interpretations do not create underdetermined answers, and that out-of-order discovery leaves the world coherent. Bind variants = `designAccessibleRoutes(room, constraints, clueReview)`; every sensory opt-out must preserve an equivalent clue path and the same required goal.

Bind failurePlaytests = `rehearseFailureStates(room, computedProof, variants, sourceEvidence)`. Simulate repeated actions and a missing/broken prop; each reachable failure requires a staff recovery route with no participant trapped. Bind operations = `packageSessionOperations(room, computedProof, variants, failurePlaytests)`. Include setup, reset, hint ladders, prop inventory and pre-session state verification. A reset is not verified until an observed readback matches every declared prop and the cleared puzzle state for the next session. The checklist alone is not a reset receipt.

Construct the complete EscapeOperationsPacket from the exact current room, computedProof, failurePlaytests, operations.setup, operations.reset, operations.hints, operations.staffRecovery and operations.checkpoint. Carry every nonempty constraints.unverifiedPropIds, clueReview.repairTargets, failure finding with disposition block, and source identity or proof mismatch into blockers with its source identifiers; retain review findings even when they do not block. Set status blocked when any such blocker exists or operations.status is blocked. Otherwise set status review because safety and enjoyment review remain a human gate. Preserve operations.checkpoint.resetVerified as returned; this design operation has no reset readback and cannot verify a reset. Include nextSessionId only if operations.checkpoint contains the authoritative allocator value. Return every declared packet field; never return only a readiness sentence.
